# Two and two, in the whole language there is: inductive types and rewrites.
#
# Nothing here says a number is a machine word. `Nat` is the type its
# declaration makes it, addition is recursion over `Succ`, and two is what
# the program builds out of its own constructors. The tiers below decide the
# representation and recognise the addition -- and then find that everything
# it adds is known, so what a target is handed is the number 4 and nothing
# to work it out with. See `opaque.fn` for where that stops.

type Nat Zero Succ(Nat)

add(a Zero) -> a
add(a Succ(k)) -> Succ(add(a k))

main!(h) -> exit!(h add(Succ(Succ(Zero)) Succ(Succ(Zero))))
